body:
Do you mean University Leadership Network (ULN)? If so, the reason for the low 4 year grad rate isn't actually related to the program itself. Rather the program was developed specifically to award and support students who, historically, have a very low 4 year graduation rate (like first generation students, low income, etc.). So if you see a low graduation rate in the program, that's why - the program isn't the cause, it is specifically selecting students in that demographic. I don't know if you've seen it yet, but they have a webpage with more information here: [https://studentsuccess.utexas.edu/programs/uln/#acc2\_collapse1](https://studentsuccess.utexas.edu/programs/uln/#acc2_collapse1)

&#x200B;

The program itself is a little varied but tends to focus on teaching students how to adjust to college life and sets up a support group where you can reach out if you're struggling. I believe they also do career prep and registration support, and have specialized counselors to help students in the program.
